# Historical basis: Fakhreddin Azimi, Iran: The Crisis of Democracy,
# 1941–1953, pp. 201–208; Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions,
# ch. 5, pp. 249–253. The recurring consultation and all effects are
# counterfactual abstractions; the scene does not posit a pre-October Front.
title: Opposition Consultation
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: opposition_consultation_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; opposition_consultation_timer = 3

= Opposition Consultation

There is no common opposition organization. Constitutional politicians,
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}
organizers, prospective independent candidates, and religious-political intermediaries
meet through overlapping personal circles, then return to institutions they
do not share.

One consultation can establish a common piece of work. It cannot give this
loose company a name, discipline, or authority it has not yet acquired.

- @consult_constitutionalists
- @consult_organizers
- @consult_intermediaries
- @return_card

@consult_constitutionalists
title: Convene the constitutional politicians
subtitle: Lawyers and former deputies seek a rule they can defend together without claiming a common organization
on-arrival: {!
Q.opposition_consultation_repeat =
    Q.opposition_consultation_last === "constitutionalists" ? 1 : 0;
Q.opposition_consultation_last = "constitutionalists";
Q.constitutional_legitimacy += Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 1 :
    (Q.constitutional_legitimacy < 65 ? 3 : 1);
Q.independent_nationalists_relation +=
    Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 1 :
    (Q.independent_nationalists_relation < 65 ? 2 : 1);
Q.parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy +=
    Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 0 :
    (Q.parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy < 65 ? 1 : 0);
if (Q.constitutional_legitimacy >= 75) Q.iran_party_dissent += 1;
!}

[? if attempt_emergency_seen = 0: The discussion settles on a limited rule:
political liberties and public authority must be judged against law and
representative government. Participants agree to repeat that case in their
own voices. ?]
[? if attempt_emergency_seen = 1: The discussion settles on a limited rule:
emergency measures, constitutional revision, and elections must each be judged
against law and representative government. Participants agree to repeat that
case in their own voices. ?]

Nobody leaves as a member of a new party. The constitutional politicians do
leave with language that makes later cooperation easier.
[? if opposition_consultation_repeat = 1:
The constitutional politicians return to the rule they already agreed. They
apply it to newer orders and objections, but the second meeting mainly keeps a
common vocabulary intact. The obstacle now lies less in drafting another
principle than in organizing people able to defend it. ?]
[? if constitutional_legitimacy >= 75: The common rule is no longer the
principal obstacle. Another consultation repeats an agreement the participants
already understand while practical questions remain unsettled. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@consult_organizers
title: Bring the party organizers together
subtitle: Existing organizations compare methods while keeping their memberships and commands separate
on-arrival: {!
Q.opposition_consultation_repeat =
    Q.opposition_consultation_last === "organizers" ? 1 : 0;
Q.opposition_consultation_last = "organizers";
Q.iran_party_organization += Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 1 :
    (Q.iran_party_organization < 70 ? 3 : 1);
Q.iran_party_relation += Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 1 :
    (Q.iran_party_relation < 70 ? 2 : 1);
Q.organizational_reach += Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 0 :
    (Q.organizational_reach < 65 ? 1 : 0);
!}

Organizers compare contact lists, meeting practices, and the routes by which
news reaches Tehran. They agree on a few common formats without pooling their
membership records or surrendering control of local workers.

The practical exchange strengthens the best-established party network.
Cooperation remains an arrangement between organizations rather than a new
organization above them.
[? if opposition_consultation_repeat = 1:
The organizers meet again with the formats and routes already agreed. They
repair missed contacts and compare recent experience, useful maintenance that
does not widen the circle or transfer anyone's membership to a common body. ?]
[? if iran_party_organization >= 75: The established organizers have already
exchanged their most useful methods. Another meeting maintains those contacts,
but does little for circles outside the party network. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@consult_intermediaries
title: Consult religious and bazaar intermediaries
subtitle: Independent intermediaries test where constitutional opposition can travel beyond party circles
on-arrival: {!
Q.opposition_consultation_repeat =
    Q.opposition_consultation_last === "intermediaries" ? 1 : 0;
Q.opposition_consultation_last = "intermediaries";
Q.religious_network_relation += Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 1 :
    (Q.religious_network_relation < 70 ? 3 : 1);
Q.religious_network_organization +=
    Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 1 :
    (Q.religious_network_organization < 70 ? 2 : 1);
Q.organizational_reach += Q.opposition_consultation_repeat ? 0 :
    (Q.organizational_reach < 65 ? 1 : 0);
!}

The intermediaries identify constitutional complaints that can be carried
through bazaar and {!<span class="term term-religious">!}religious
networks{!</span>!} without asking those networks to accept a party program.
They also state where their own authority and priorities remain separate.

A wider channel of cooperation opens. It belongs to the intermediaries who
maintain it, not to a central opposition staff.
[? if opposition_consultation_repeat = 1:
The intermediaries carry replies through the channel already opened and
identify where recent demands have met resistance. The relationship is kept
alive, but another consultation neither enlarges their independent authority
nor places it under opposition command. ?]
[? if religious_network_relation >= 75: The channel is now familiar to both
sides. Further consultation preserves it, but does not erase the separate
authority or priorities of the intermediaries. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
